{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ge2xjbemgcesb37l4wn4chtoz6e7xmhracwdfxbpsoog35yrx4ca","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The complete C library is translated to Rust and verified.\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src/` is a single 956-line file: the **stb_ds** dynamic-array / hash-map implementation (arrays, binary-key hashmaps, string-key hashmaps with 4 key-storage modes, siphash-2-4 + string hash, string arena) plus two test helpers (`strkey`, `arr_push`). The public header only declares `arr_push`; everything else is exported via the `extern` prototypes at the top of `lib.c`.\n\n## Deliverables\n- `Cargo.toml` — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`, name `translated_rust` (same `.so` name as the C build)\n- `src/lib.rs` — 1181 lines, all 16 public functions with `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"`\n\n## Symbol parity (completion gate)\n`nm -D --defined-only` diff between the C `.so` (built with cmake) and the Rust `.so` is **empty — 16/16 symbols, no extras**:\n`stbds_arrgrowf, stbds_arrfreef, stbds_rand_seed, stbds_hash_string, stbds_hash_bytes, stbds_hmget_key, stbds_hmget_key_ts, stbds_hmput_default, stbds_hmput_key, stbds_hmdel_key, stbds_shmode_func, stbds_hmfree_func, stbds_stralloc, stbds_strreset, strkey, arr_push`\n\n## Behavioral verification (differential, not self-reported)\nI compiled **one** driver binary per suite and ran it twice, swapping only `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` between the C and Rust `.so` (identical machine code in the driver, so evaluation order can't differ). The drivers reuse the real stb_ds macros extracted from `lib.c`.\n\n| Suite | Coverage | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `drv` | full macro API: arrays, int/long-long/struct-key maps, all 3 string modes, arena, defaults, edge cases | 6492 lines identical |\n| `fz` | xorshift-random insert/get/delete fuzz (int + 2 string modes), 4 KB hashes, 65 KB arena strings, array stress | 23549 lines identical |\n| `dr` | raw exported functions called directly (NULL args, `shmode_func` modes 0–3, mode>1, `arrgrowf` odd elemsizes) | 457 lines identical |\n| `st` | **internal** `stbds_hash_index` state incl. the global seed PRNG evolution across tables | 30 lines identical |\n| `bk` | **raw bucket dumps** (`hash[]`/`index[]` for every slot) through grow/tombstone/shrink/rehash | 15850 lines identical |\n\nAll exit codes match too (including one suite where a deliberate API misuse segfaults in *both* libraries identically).\n\n## Fidelity notes\n- Allocations go through libc `realloc`/`free`, so pointers handed to callers stay compatible with the `STBDS_FREE` in caller-side macros.\n- `#[repr(C)]` structs with compile-time `assert!`s pinning sizes (32/128/16/24/104) to the C layout.\n- C quirks preserved, not \"fixed\": the `int` sign-extension in siphash's `d[3] << 24` / `case 4:` paths, the missing `temp_key` write in `hmput_key`'s wrapped probe loop, `stbds_arrfreef(NULL)` dereferencing a bogus header, `hash ^= hash ^ rot(...)` written literally, x86 shift-masking in the arena block sizing, and all wrapping arithmetic.\n- `c_src/` is untouched (md5sums recorded)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1219,"cache_read_input_tokens":119135,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1219,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f725afb-7768-499d-90aa-8caf28b979bc","uuid":"fcacdde7-be9a-45bd-a567-2bf988cf23c7","timestamp":"2026-08-20T02:42:22.040Z"}
